## Summary

**Key idea:** Compactify $\mathbb{R}^3$ to $S^3$, where the line $L$ plus $\infty$ becomes an unknotted circle $C$. Then $\mathbb{R}^3 \setminus (L \cup \{p\}) \cong (S^1 \times \mathbb{R}^2) \setminus \{\text{pt}\}$ (open solid torus minus a point).

**Main steps:**
1. **Van Kampen** gives $\pi_1 \cong \mathbb{Z}$ (the $S^1$ factor survives; the loop around the removed point is killed).
2. The **universal cover** is $\mathbb{R}^3$ minus $\mathbb{Z}$-many isolated points on a line (the preimage of $p$ under the covering map $\mathbb{R}^3 \to S^1 \times \mathbb{R}^2$).
3. The universal cover is **simply connected** (loops in 3D can be perturbed off 0-dimensional obstacles), so Hurewicz gives $\pi_2 \cong H_2$.
4. **Alexander duality** on the compact set $A = \{(n,0,0)\} \cup \{\infty\} \subset S^3$ (a convergent sequence) yields $H_2 \cong \check{\widetilde{H}}^0(A) \cong \bigoplus_{\mathbb{Z}} \mathbb{Z}$.

$$\boxed{\pi_2\!\left(\mathbb{R}^3 \setminus (L \cup \{p\})\right) \cong \bigoplus_{n \in \mathbb{Z}} \mathbb{Z}}$$

As a $\mathbb{Z}[\pi_1]$-module ($\pi_1 \cong \mathbb{Z}$), this is $\mathbb{Z}[t, t^{-1}]$ — free of rank 1 over the group ring, generated by a sphere around $p$, with the deck transformation shifting between the countably many lifts.
